            <ArticleTitle>[A man with recurrent, episodic abdominal pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>D1453</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 56-year-old man with episodic abdominal pain was evaluated for acute left-side abdominal pain. CT scans showed an alternating location of the liver. This phenomenon, in which the liver is freely displaced along the transverse axis around the inferior vena cava, is called 'wandering liver'.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
